WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.774
This practice asks you to keep every employee row
while adding department

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:09.139
and company averages That wording tells us not to
collapse the result

00:00:09.165 --> 00:00:15.135
with GROUP BY Instead use window functions One

00:00:15.161 --> 00:00:19.648
average should use a department partition The other
should use the full

00:00:19.674 --> 00:00:25.203
set of remaining rows Run the starter example after
completing it

00:00:25.216 --> 00:00:30.350
and inspect several employees from the same
department Their department average should

00:00:30.376 --> 00:00:35.989
match while their individual salary values remain
different Then

00:00:36.015 --> 00:00:41.343
compare that with the company-wide average This is a
useful test for

00:00:41.369 --> 00:00:45.264
deciding between GROUP BY and windows if the
original detail rows must

00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:49.158
remain visible a window function is often the better
analytical tool
